, "pos": [-1144.5185546875, 2472.79541015625], "widgets_values": ["A single antique-looking hardbound book stands upright in a three-quarter view, positioned slightly below center and angled so both the front cover and the narrow right spine area are visible. The book occupies most of the frame, roughly two-thirds of the image width, with a thick rectangular form and subtly warped perspective caused by its leaning posture. Its cover is dark aged brown, resembling distressed leather or leather-like material, with a matte, scratched, grainy texture distributed unevenly across the surface. Raised border molding runs around the perimeter of the cover, forming inner rectangular frames with thin ridges and shadow lines. The front-cover panel is plain and unlettered, showing natural wear marks, shallow dents, rubbed edges, and lighter scuffed patches especially near the middle. At the top edge and partly through the bottom opening between the covers, a stack of aged cream-colored pages is visible, aligned horizontally and slightly fanned by perspective. The page edges look yellowed and fibrous, with many thin parallel sheet layers discernible. Blue ruled lines run continuously across the pages, evenly spaced and delicate, suggesting a notebook or diary rather than a printed volume. A similar line of blue rulings can also be seen peeking out along the left inner side where the pages turn away from the viewer. Small portions of stacked paper extend beyond the cover edges at the far left of the front page block and near the lower-right margin, emphasizing the book’s thickness and handmade construction. The outer board structure appears sturdy, with beige-brown wooden or cardboard layering visible around the spine, hinge areas, and page blocks. Both visible corners of the cover are rounded and heavily softened by age; the top-right and lower-left front corners curl upward slightly, exposing rough torn paper layers underneath. These curled corners have irregular wavy edges, frayed fibers, darker staining, and ragged strands hanging loosely over the main cover. A twisted cord or wrapped thread detail is visible around the lower-left corner of the front cover, passing diagonally across the junction of page and cover as part of the traditional binding. Shadows collect inside these curls, creating strong contrast against the smoother flat cover. On the right side, the spine region shows additional bands of cream page stacks emerging beyond the brown cover at intervals, indicating either multi-volume layering or decorative exposed paper sections. Subtle embossed groove-like details appear near the spine, including short segmented bands running vertically along the rear joint. Soft directional light enters from above-left, producing gentle highlights across the textured cover and pronounced but diffuse shadows beneath the book and within the deep curves of the damaged corners. The ground plane beneath the object is lightly colored and minimally defined, blending into the same muted tan-gray environment as the backdrop. The background is a smooth neutral plaster-like wall with a faint mottled texture, tonal gradients ranging from warm gray to taupe, and very little depth information. This minimal setting keeps attention entirely on the weathered object. The overall composition feels like a carefully lit still-life photograph with realistic materials, high-detail macro-style rendering, subdued color grading, and a restrained vintage atmosphere."], "inputs": [{"shape": 7, "name": "anything", "link": 770, "label": "输入任何", "type": "*", "localized_name": "anything"}], "flags": {}, "id": 499, "type": "easy showAnything", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "easy showAnything"}, "order": 9}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "rewritten_prompt", "links": [769, 770], "label": "rewritten_prompt", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "rewritten_prompt"}, {"name": "pe_result", "links": [], "label": "pe_result", "type": "PE_RESULT"